# Trivy ignore list for the alpine, slim and noble images (homelab-runbooks #465, D3).
#
# Used by both Trivy scans: the pull-request scan in
# .github/workflows/lint-build-boot-test.yml and the post-publish scan job in
# .github/workflows/sync-predbat.yml. Both alert on fixable CRITICAL and HIGH
# findings only (severity CRITICAL,HIGH, ignore-unfixed).
#
# Only add an entry for a deliberate, reviewed exception: a comment line with the
# variant(s) and the reason, then the finding on its own line:
#
#   # <variant(s)>: <reason>
#   <CVE or rule id> exp:<review-by date YYYY-MM-DD>
#
# Trivy stops ignoring the entry after the exp: date, so the scan alerts again
# and the exception has to be reviewed and either renewed or removed.
#
# Example (not active):
#   # noble: only in a build-time package, not reachable at runtime
#   CVE-2026-00000 exp:2027-02-01
#
# No exceptions at present.
